  "goodToKnow": "Die Novelle has two meanings. In literature, it's a novella, a key German genre with a single unheard-of event (eine unerhörte Begebenheit, as Goethe put it), like Storm's Der Schimmelreiter. A full novel is der Roman. In politics, it's an amendment to a law: die Novelle des Infektionsschutzgesetzes; novellieren means to amend. Both come from Latin novus (new). Plural: die Novellen."
